# Tracey Bootstrap Compiler Documentation

This directory contains the documentation for the Tracey bootstrap compiler
(`traceyc`) and its experimental internal toolchain (assembler and linker).

## Contents

- `architecture.md` — overall compiler architecture and pipeline.
- `build.md` — build instructions, configuration, silent build.
- `lexer.md` — lexical analysis specification.
- `parser.md` — parser and AST specification.
- `semantic.md` — semantic analysis and type checking.
- `codegen.md` — code generation (AArch64).
- `assembler.md` — internal AArch64 assembler.
- `linker.md` — internal ELF64 AArch64 linker.
- `usage.md` — end-to-end usage examples.
- `testing.md` — running and adding tests.
- `maintenance.md` — coding style, formatting, and maintenance.

## Project status

Tracey is in the bootstrap stage. The compiler currently supports a broad
subset of a C-like language: functions (including `void` and variadic
declarations), local variables of many integer and floating-point types,
basic `typedef` aliases, pointers and fixed-size arrays, file-scope `struct`
definitions with local struct variables and member access, `if`/`else`,
`while`, `do`/`while`, `for`, `switch`/`case`/`default`, `break`,
`continue`, `goto` and labels, arithmetic, comparisons, logical and bitwise
operators, ternary `?:`, prefix and postfix `++`/`--`, `sizeof`, assignment
and compound assignment, and `return`. Some features keep deliberate
bootstrap limits: `sizeof` returns 8 for every scalar type, `switch` cases
do not fall through, `typedef` covers basic type aliases only, and struct
support is limited to scalar and nested-struct members (no arrays,
initializers, parameters, return values, or pointers). The internal
assembler and linker support AArch64 Linux only.

The compiler runs the full pipeline itself: it preprocesses, lexes,
parses, type-checks, generates assembly, then (unless asked for assembly
only) assembles and links the result into an executable. By default the
executable is named `a.out`.
